{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/654541-demon-translation-guide-deathgrip","id":654541,"title":"Demon Translation Guide: Deathgrip","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-06T16:36:14-07:00","id":654541,"title":"Demon Translation Guide: Deathgrip","content":"I'm diving through the Demonic Form abilities that can be ported over from Fallen, and I've come across this. I referred to my copy of DtF and I have a question.<br /> <br /> Am I understanding correctly, that this basically allows any Demon with this process to circumvent death with no roll as long as they are in demonic form, or have Deathgrip manifested as part of a partial transformation? And the only cost for doing so is a dot of willpower in the worst case scenario where their body is no longer intact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:03:57-07:00","id":654581,"title":"","content":"That's mostly right, but rising from Deathgrip also strips your Aether reserves empty. And remember that partially manifesting a demonic form ability still produces a visible transmutation of the body. A deathgrip system is going to make you look weird enough to risk compromise, such as the grainy flesh suggested in the Translation Guide. Additionally, changing form to get rid of it and look fully human costs Aether, so if you're not in full demonic form when you die, you'll have to adopt it to pay the Aether cost to turn back when you rise.<br /> <br /> Still super useful. If you're wondering how to narratively threaten a demon with Deathgrip, well, a) it only protects the demon, not his friends, allies or loved ones; and b) it doesn't help against non-lethal incapacitation, which is one of the God-Machine's favored tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T23:51:29-07:00","id":654821,"title":"","content":"I hadn't even thought of all the complications coming back without Aether is likely to provoke. And being permanently incapacitated can definitely provoke some &quot;I have no mouth but I must scream' horror.<br /> <br /> I'm not too concerned about the power level of this Form Ability since there are Exploits that provide a similar level of protection, but I wanted to make sure I wasn't misinterpreting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}